The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    private function sortJoinedTypes(string $types): string
    {
        $types = array_filter(
            Preg::split('/([^|<]+(?:<.*>)?)/', $types, -1, PREG_SPLIT_DELIM_CAPTURE | PREG_SPLIT_NO_EMPTY),
            static function (string $value) {
                return '|' !== $value;
            }
        );

        return implode('|', $this->sortTypes($types));
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `PhpCsFixer\Tests\Fixer\Phpdoc\PhpdocTypesOrderFixerTest::testFixWithNullFirst with data set #27`:
            
```php
    public function testFixWithNullFirst(string $expected, ?string $input = null): void
    {
        $this->fixer->configure([
            'sort_algorithm' => 'none',
            'null_adjustment' => 'always_first',
        ]);

        $this->doTest($expected, $input);
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Code build on expected code must not change.
Failed asserting that two strings are identical.
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
private function sortJoinedTypes(string $types): string
{
    $types = array_filter(
        preg_split('/([^|<]+(?:<.*>)?)/', $types, -1, PREG_SPLIT_DELIM_CAPTURE | PREG_SPLIT_NO_EMPTY),
        static function (string $value) {
            return '|'!== $value;
        }
    );

    // Ensure null is always first if present
    $hasNull = false;
    $types = array_map(function ($type) use (&$hasNull) {
        if ($type === 'null') {
            $hasNull = true;
            return null; // Temporarily set to null for sorting
        }
        return $type;
    }, $types);

    $sortedTypes = $this->sortTypes(array_filter($types, function ($type) {
        return $type!== null;
    }));

    if ($hasNull) {
        array_unshift($sortedTypes, 'null');
    }

    return implode('|', $sortedTypes);
}
```
